**Read:** [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), full conduction, fins, convection and exchanger models; [Nano-to-Macro Transport Processes — MIT 2.57](../sources/Nano-to-Macro-Transport-MIT-2-57.lingua#r_1YF7TD689ZRGQ51D4B3NGVHZQG), scale-dependent transport; [Time-domain thermoreflectance — Jiang, Qian and Yang](../sources/Time-Domain-Thermoreflectance-Jiang-Qian-Yang.lingua#r_7ZHR7DG99WYCCG8J21HTKE9TMS), material/interface measurement; [Heat Pipe Design Handbook, Volume I — Brennan and Kroliczek](../sources/Heat-Pipe-Design-Handbook-Brennan-Kroliczek.lingua#r_08JYCA7B2K6B8E5490DSJYQJFA), relevant complete cooling-link design method.

Trace energy generation from a device's active region through films, substrate, package, interfaces, spreader, cooler and ambient. Define the spatial and temporal distribution of dissipation. A single junction-to-ambient resistance represents particular boundary conditions and cannot automatically predict a different board, mounting or airflow.

Combine a compact thermal network with resolved regions where spreading, interface resistance or transient gradients matter. Include uncertain contacts and fluid conditions. Check both steady duty and pulsed loads; thermal capacity can delay a peak without removing the energy eventually discharged.

Compare a continuum package model with the scale at which carrier or interface effects require deeper treatment. Specify a measurement that can challenge the predicted internal temperature, accounting for the observable's relation to that temperature. The full chip fabrication, packaging and electronics subjects supply their own processes; this Record makes their thermal dependencies explicit.

